# Staged artefacts, not source — see README.md ("Getting the model").
# Both come straight out of birdnet.load("acoustic", "3.0", "onnx"), so they are
# reproducible in two lines and do not belong in history. Unlike
# examples/densenet_onnx/model/densenet_onnx.onnx (31 MB, committed), this model
# is 517 MB — five times GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit — so a push carrying
# it is rejected outright, and this repo is mirrored to both GitLab and GitHub.
model.onnx
labels.txt

# The soundscape(s) the example runs against — the dataset, restaged per run.
*.wav

# Superseded fp16 export (271 MB) and its label list, kept only to reproduce
# pre-2026-09-07 numbers. README says to delete them once nothing depends on the
# old confidences. Note the backup deliberately avoids the .onnx extension: a
# second *.onnx here makes find_model "select first match" with only a warning.
*.bak
